On the nonnegative integers, S={(x,y):y=x+1}. Find its reflexive transitive closure. GFG prints the domain {0,1,2,…}; GateForum omits the ellipsis and prints {0,1,2}, for which the same order condition applies restricted to that finite domain.
Options:
(A) {(x,y):y>x}
(B) {(x,y):y≥x}
(C) {(x,y):y<x}
(D) {(x,y):y≤x}

Let S={{1,2},{1,2,3},{1,3,5},{1,2,4},{1,2,3,4,5}}, ordered by containment. Which listed minimal collection of sets must be adjoined to make a complete lattice? “Necessary” is interpreted as the minimal sufficient offered augmentation, not a claim excluding every other possible bottom element.
Options:
(A) {1}
(B) {1} and {2,3}
(C) {1} and {1,3}
(D) {1}, {1,3}, {1,2,3,4}, {1,2,3,5}
